 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Totally normal. Lots of people never get over it. The best antidote is practice. Start where you always stop, at the store or park. Keep it short at first and maybe switch to light roads. Once you feel confident, you can take the busy ones. The key is usually stopping halfway off at shop or park, and starting there if you' late or stressed. People rarely overtake on quiet roads. Start using pulleys to get your bag off completely and you' be surprised how much it helps.",
